-- חוזר לבעלויות תשס"ח/1 — ניכוי שכר מעובדי הוראה בשל שביתות מלאות בשנת הלימודים תשס"ח (23.10.2007)
-- Salary is deducted for the days and hours of the secondary teachers'
-- strike, under the takanon's rule on unjustified absence (section 1.25.14):
-- below 10% of the monthly quota only from the hours actually taught, above
-- it also from the education and matriculation hours and the role supplements.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT common

§ `ניכוי שכר בשל שביתות מלאות תשס"ח`

-- akn:hc_1/p1 akn:hc_1/p2 akn:hc_1/p3 akn:hc_1/p4 akn:hc_1/p5 akn:hc_1/p6 akn:hc_1/p7 akn:hc_1/p8 akn:hc_1/p9 akn:hc_1/p10 The letterhead, title, date, addressee, greeting and subject line; no rule.

-- akn:hc_1/p11 The background: from September 2007 the secondary teachers' organisation held full strikes in secondary schools and seminaries.

@desc One teaching employee's month of the strike, as far as this circular asks about it.
DECLARE `strike month` HAS
    `fixed monthly quota in hours`              IS A NUMBER  @desc the employee's fixed monthly quota of work (מכסת עבודתו הקבועה)
    `hours absent on strike`                    IS A NUMBER  @desc hours of the fixed timetable missed by taking part in the strike
    `value of one teaching hour`                IS A NUMBER  @desc an input, not set by this circular
    `education and matriculation-preparation pay` IS A NUMBER @desc the month's pay for education hours and matriculation-preparation hours
    `role percentage supplements`               IS A NUMBER  @desc the month's percentage supplements paid for roles

DECLARE `strike action` IS ONE OF
    `deduct the salary` HAS `amount deducted` IS A NUMBER
    `deduct from the standing payments` HAS `hours deducted` IS A NUMBER

-- ¶12: salary is deducted from every teacher who took part, by the days and
-- hours of their part; ¶17: the owning body deducts it, by the teacher's
-- fixed timetable at the school — the hours missed are counted on it.
@ref akn:hc_1/p12 akn:hc_1/p17
GIVEN m IS A `strike month`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `strike action`
DECIDE `the owning body deducts the strike salary` m IS
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
    MUST  `deduct the salary` amount
          PROVIDED amount EQUALS `salary to deduct` m

GIVEN m IS A `strike month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `deduction for the hours taught` m IS
    m's `hours absent on strike` TIMES m's `value of one teaching hour`

GIVEN m IS A `strike month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `share of the quota absent` m IS
    m's `hours absent on strike` DIVIDED BY m's `fixed monthly quota in hours`

-- ¶13: the rule is the takanon's on unjustified absence (section 1.25.14),
-- restated here in ¶14–16 (א) and ב.
-- ¶14–16 (א): below 10% of the quota, only the hours actually taught; not
-- the education or matriculation hours, nor the role percentage supplements.
@ref akn:hc_1/p13 akn:hc_1/p14 akn:hc_1/p15 akn:hc_1/p16
GIVEN m IS A `strike month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `deduction when the absence is below 10%` m IS
    `deduction for the hours taught` m

GIVEN m IS A `strike month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `absence below 10%` m IF
    `share of the quota absent` m LESS THAN 10%

-- ב: above 10%, also the proportional part of the unjustified absence from
-- the education and matriculation hours and the role supplements.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_b akn:hc_1__para_b/p2
GIVEN m IS A `strike month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `deduction when the absence is above 10%` m IS
    `deduction for the hours taught` m
    PLUS `deduction from the supplements` m

GIVEN m IS A `strike month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `absence above 10%` m IF
    `share of the quota absent` m GREATER THAN 10%

GIVEN m IS A `strike month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `deduction from the supplements` m IS
    `share of the quota absent` m
    TIMES (m's `education and matriculation-preparation pay` PLUS m's `role percentage supplements`)

§§ `The amount deducted, as read`

-- F-2007-08_tashsach_01-a: exactly 10% is neither "less than" nor "more
-- than". The reading adopted: the wider deduction needs the absence to
-- EXCEED 10%, so at exactly 10% only the hours taught are deducted.
@export The salary an owning body deducts from a teaching employee for one month of the 2007-08 strike
GIVEN m IS A `strike month` @desc the employee's month
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `salary to deduct` m IS
    IF `absence above 10%` m
    THEN `deduction when the absence is above 10%` m
    ELSE `deduction when the absence is below 10%` m

§§ `The Ministry's deduction`

-- ¶18: the Ministry deducts from its current standing payments (מת"מ) to
-- the owning bodies, by the budgeted hours of the striking institutions and
-- the strike dates. The hours are the Ministry's figure: an input.
@ref akn:hc_1/p18
GIVEN `budgeted hours of the striking institutions` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `strike action`
DECIDE `the Ministry deducts from its payments` `budgeted hours of the striking institutions` IS
    PARTY `the Ministry of Education`
    MUST  `deduct from the standing payments` h
          PROVIDED h EQUALS `budgeted hours of the striking institutions`

-- akn:conclusions The sign-off and signature; no rule.

§§ `Worked examples`

-- A quota of 100 hours, hour value 100, supplements 2,000 —
-- placeholders.
`ten hours of a hundred` MEANS
    `strike month` WITH
        `fixed monthly quota in hours`                IS 100
        `hours absent on strike`                      IS 10
        `value of one teaching hour`                  IS 100
        `education and matriculation-preparation pay` IS 1500
        `role percentage supplements`                 IS 500

`twenty hours of a hundred` MEANS
    `strike month` WITH
        `fixed monthly quota in hours`                IS 100
        `hours absent on strike`                      IS 20
        `value of one teaching hour`                  IS 100
        `education and matriculation-preparation pay` IS 1500
        `role percentage supplements`                 IS 500

`five hours of a hundred` MEANS
    `strike month` WITH
        `fixed monthly quota in hours`                IS 100
        `hours absent on strike`                      IS 5
        `value of one teaching hour`                  IS 100
        `education and matriculation-preparation pay` IS 1500
        `role percentage supplements`                 IS 500

#ASSERT `salary to deduct` `five hours of a hundred` EQUALS 500
#ASSERT `salary to deduct` `twenty hours of a hundred` EQUALS 2400
#ASSERT `salary to deduct` `ten hours of a hundred` EQUALS 1000

-- F-2007-08_tashsach_01-a: an absence of exactly 10% is decided by neither
-- (א) nor ב.
`an absence of exactly 10% falls in neither rule` MEANS
        NOT `absence below 10%` `ten hours of a hundred`
    AND NOT `absence above 10%` `ten hours of a hundred`
#ASSERT `an absence of exactly 10% falls in neither rule`

#TRACE `the owning body deducts the strike salary` `twenty hours of a hundred` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body` DOES `deduct the salary` 2400 AT 1
